--
The clang builtin __make_integer_seq materialises
integer_sequence<unsigned long, 0, 1, 2>, which is matched by a
partial specialization deducing the pack _Ip..., and a binary fold
over _Ip in a STATIC member initializer must evaluate to 3
(N5008 [temp.deduct.type], [expr.prim.fold]/2).  CBMC leaves the fold
partially expanded ("in expression '<<expr:static_cast>> + 0'") and
drops the enclosing body.  Found round 130 while kerneling the
cpp20_ranges_basic_libcxx reduced3 artifact; suspected shared root
with the __perfect_forward operator() trailing-decltype chain
(`get<_Idx>(__bound_args_)...`, the artifact's remaining layer).
Clang-only builtin: g++ does not accept this file.
